Cost and recommendation
The next focused fix round is estimated at 40-75 minutes for the four findings,
followed by about 10-15 minutes for an independent review; a clean result still
requires a separate final review. These are estimates, not measured promises.
The first reviewer took about ten minutes and used 104,875 tokens.
Recommend continuing with all four findings: each addresses the requested
launcher contract or preservation of existing review rules. Leave the unproven
large-policy performance question for separate triage. Firstmate owns the
continuation decision; this worker has not accepted or started any fix.

Private note cleanup after acceptance
data/codex-review-loop.md was not edited. Its raw reviewer/fixer launch recipes,
manual prompt concatenation and model flags, dated runtime override pointer,
root-level round/report layout, and duplicated round-boundary/report-completion
instructions are now covered by the bundled script and generated review text.
Firstmate can trim those parts after the outstanding findings are settled.
